{
  "id": "b1.g14", "level": "B1", "kind": "grammar",
  "title": "Pronouns review",
  "subtitle": "mij or me, hen or hun, zich, zelf, elkaar, men and je",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "b1.g14.l1", "title": "Personal pronouns: stressed or unstressed, hen or hun", "kind": "grammar",
      "explain": [
        { "type": "p", "text": "Most personal pronouns have a **stressed** and an **unstressed** form. Use the **stressed** form for **emphasis or contrast** and **after a preposition**: *Ik wacht op **jou**.* *Dit cadeau is voor **mij**.* *Hij belt **mij**, niet jou.* Use the **unstressed** form in ordinary sentences: *Ik bel **je** morgen.* *Hij ziet **me**.*" },
        { "type": "table", "head": ["person", "subject", "object (stressed)", "object (unstressed)"], "rows": [["ik", "ik", "mij", "me"], ["jij", "jij / je", "jou", "je"], ["hij", "hij", "hem", "hem"], ["zij (she)", "zij / ze", "haar", "haar"], ["wij", "wij / we", "ons", "ons"], ["zij (they)", "zij / ze", "hen / hun", "ze"]] },
        { "type": "p", "text": "For **they / them** the norm has two forms: **hen** for a direct object and after a preposition (*Ik ken hen. Ik praat met hen.*), and **hun** for an indirect object, *to them* (*Ik geef hun het boek.*). Many speakers mix them up. **Ze** is always safe: *Ik ken ze. Ik geef ze het boek.*" },
        { "type": "ex", "nl": "Ik wacht op jou.", "en": "I am waiting for you." },
        { "type": "ex", "nl": "Ik geef hun het boek.", "en": "I give them the book." },
        { "type": "tip", "text": "*Hun* is also the possessive *their*: *hun huis*. As a personal pronoun it means *to them*." }
      ],
      "items": [
        { "type": "choice", "q": "Dit cadeau is voor ___. (me)", "options": ["mij", "ik", "mijn"], "answer": 0 },
        { "type": "choice", "q": "Ik wacht op ___. (you, informal)", "options": ["jou", "jij", "jouw"], "answer": 0 },
        { "type": "choice", "q": "Ik ken ___ goed. (the colleagues, direct object)", "options": ["hen", "hun", "zij"], "answer": 0 },
        { "type": "choice", "q": "Ik geef ___ het boek. (to them, the norm)", "options": ["hun", "hen", "zij"], "answer": 0 },
        { "type": "choice", "q": "Which is the unstressed form of the subject *jij*?", "options": ["je", "jou", "jouw"], "answer": 0 },
        { "type": "gap", "text": "Hij belt ___, niet jou. (me, stressed)", "answers": ["mij"], "en": "He is calling me, not you." },
        { "type": "gap", "text": "Ik praat met ___. (them)", "answers": ["hen", "ze"], "en": "I am talking with them." },
        { "type": "gap", "text": "Ik geef ___ een cadeau. (to them)", "answers": ["hun", "ze"], "en": "I give them a present." },
        { "type": "gap", "text": "Dit is voor ___. (you, informal)", "answers": ["jou", "je"], "en": "This is for you." },
        { "type": "gap", "text": "Ik zie ___ niet. (him)", "answers": ["hem"], "en": "I don't see him." },
        { "type": "gap", "text": "Zij geeft ___ een boek. (to him)", "answers": ["hem"], "en": "She gives him a book." },
        { "type": "transform", "q": "Ik ken de collega's.", "instruction": "Replace *de collega's* with hen.", "answers": ["Ik ken hen"] },
        { "type": "transform", "q": "Ik geef de kinderen een cadeau.", "instruction": "Replace *de kinderen* with hun.", "answers": ["Ik geef hun een cadeau", "Ik geef ze een cadeau"] },
        { "type": "transform", "q": "Ik wacht op Anna.", "instruction": "Replace *Anna* with a pronoun.", "answers": ["Ik wacht op haar"] },
        { "type": "transform", "q": "Ik bel de buurman.", "instruction": "Replace *de buurman* with a pronoun.", "answers": ["Ik bel hem"] },
        { "type": "order", "answer": "Ik wacht op jou.", "en": "I am waiting for you." },
        { "type": "order", "answer": "Dit cadeau is voor mij.", "en": "This present is for me." },
        { "type": "order", "answer": "Ik geef hun het boek.", "en": "I give them the book." },
        { "type": "order", "answer": "Ik praat vaak met hen.", "en": "I often talk with them." },
        { "type": "translate", "en": "I am waiting for you.", "answers": ["Ik wacht op jou", "Ik wacht op je", "Ik wacht op u"] },
        { "type": "translate", "en": "I know them.", "answers": ["Ik ken hen", "Ik ken ze"] },
        { "type": "translate", "en": "I give them the book.", "answers": ["Ik geef hun het boek", "Ik geef ze het boek", "Ik geef het boek aan hen", "Ik geef het boek aan ze"] },
        { "type": "match", "pairs": [["mij", "stressed: me"], ["me", "unstressed: me"], ["hen", "them (object / after a preposition)"], ["hun", "to them (indirect object)"]] }
      ],
      "sources": [
