    {
      "id": "b1.g14.l3", "title": "men, je, het, dit and dat", "kind": "grammar",
      "explain": [
        { "type": "p", "text": "To talk about **people in general** Dutch has **men** (formal, mostly written: *Men mag hier niet roken.*) and **je** (spoken, *you* in general: *Je mag hier niet roken.*). **Men** is always a **singular subject** and has **zich** as its reflexive: *Men moet zich aanmelden.* *Ze* (*they*) is also common in speech: *Ze zeggen dat het koud wordt.*" },
        { "type": "p", "text": "**Het** can be a **dummy subject** with no meaning: *Het regent. Het is koud. Het gaat goed.* To point at something use **dit / dat**, which stay the same before a plural verb: *Wat is dit? Dat zijn mijn schoenen.* Before a noun use **dit / dat** with het-words and **deze / die** with de-words and plurals." },
        { "type": "table", "head": ["word", "use", "example"], "rows": [["men", "formal, general subject", "Men mag hier niet roken."], ["je", "spoken, general you", "Je mag hier niet roken."], ["het", "dummy subject", "Het regent."], ["dit / dat", "pointing at things", "Dat zijn mijn schoenen."]] },
        { "type": "ex", "nl": "Men moet zich aanmelden bij de balie.", "en": "One must register at the desk." },
        { "type": "ex", "nl": "Dit zijn mijn ouders.", "en": "These are my parents." },
        { "type": "tip", "text": "*Men* needs a **singular verb**: *men mag*, not *men mogen*." }
      ],
      "items": [
        { "type": "choice", "q": "___ mag hier niet roken. (formal sign)", "options": ["Men", "Hen", "Het"], "answer": 0 },
        { "type": "choice", "q": "In Nederland moet ___ een fietslicht hebben. (spoken, general)", "options": ["je", "jou", "hun"], "answer": 0 },
        { "type": "choice", "q": "___ regent vandaag.", "options": ["Het", "Hij", "Dat"], "answer": 0 },
        { "type": "choice", "q": "Dat ___ mijn schoenen.", "options": ["zijn", "is", "heeft"], "answer": 0 },
        { "type": "choice", "q": "Which sentence is correct?", "options": ["Men moet zich aanmelden.", "Men moeten zich aanmelden."], "answer": 0 },
        { "type": "gap", "text": "___ zegt dat het morgen mooi weer wordt. (formal: one says)", "answers": ["Men"], "en": "They say that the weather will be nice tomorrow." },
        { "type": "gap", "text": "Als ___ in Nederland woont, moet je een zorgverzekering hebben.", "answers": ["je"], "en": "If you live in the Netherlands, you must have health insurance." },
        { "type": "gap", "text": "___ is koud buiten.", "answers": ["Het"], "en": "It is cold outside." },
        { "type": "gap", "text": "___ zijn mijn ouders. (these)", "answers": ["Dit", "Dat"], "en": "These are my parents." },
        { "type": "gap", "text": "Wat is ___? — Dat is een fiets. (this)", "answers": ["dit"], "en": "What is this? — That is a bike." },
        { "type": "gap", "text": "Ik weet ___ niet. (it)", "answers": ["het"], "en": "I don't know." },
        { "type": "transform", "q": "Je mag hier niet roken.", "instruction": "Make it formal with men: Men ...", "answers": ["Men mag hier niet roken"] },
        { "type": "transform", "q": "Men zegt dat het koud wordt.", "instruction": "Say it with ze: Ze ...", "answers": ["Ze zeggen dat het koud wordt"] },
        { "type": "transform", "q": "De regen valt.", "instruction": "Use the dummy subject: Het ...", "answers": ["Het regent"] },
        { "type": "transform", "q": "Je moet je aanmelden.", "instruction": "Make it formal with men: Men ...", "answers": ["Men moet zich aanmelden"] },
        { "type": "order", "answer": "Men mag hier niet roken.", "en": "One may not smoke here." },
        { "type": "order", "answer": "Het regent al de hele dag.", "en": "It has been raining all day." },
        { "type": "order", "answer": "Dat zijn mijn schoenen.", "en": "Those are my shoes." },
        { "type": "order", "answer": "Je moet je paspoort laten zien.", "en": "You have to show your passport." },
        { "type": "translate", "en": "One may not smoke here.", "answers": ["Men mag hier niet roken", "Je mag hier niet roken", "Hier mag niet gerookt worden"] },
        { "type": "translate", "en": "It is raining.", "answers": ["Het regent"] },
        { "type": "translate", "en": "Those are my shoes.", "answers": ["Dat zijn mijn schoenen"] },
        { "type": "match", "pairs": [["men", "formal general subject"], ["je", "spoken general you"], ["Het regent.", "dummy subject het"], ["Dat zijn …", "pointing at several things"]] }
      ],
      "sources": [
